From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:28:29 -0500
Subject: feat: Ctrl-Tab changes the tab when Ctrl is let go (S-547)

GitHub issue 123; the owner, 2026-11-18: planned. Holding Ctrl and pressing
Tab used to show each tab of the run as the strip stepped to it, so every
page stepped past flashed by. Now a step moves the strip's highlight, and
the tab changes when the run ends: when Ctrl (the chord's held keys,
shortcuts Z18) is let go, a click lands, a key without the chord's
modifiers arrives, or the window stops being active (switcher X3). Escape
leaves the tab the run began on, which never changed. A tap, Ctrl-Tab
pressed and let go at once, still shows the tab used before (X2), at the
release. The command bar's "Go to the Most Recent Tab" ends its run at
once, as before. Previews of the pages in the strip are not part of this.

SpaceModel::CycleRecent() moves the run's position only; EndCycle() shows
the tab the run reached, if it is still open, and records it as used.

Tests: SpaceWindowTest.CtrlTabWalksRecentTabsOfTheActiveSpace,
CtrlTabTapGoesToPreviousTab and CtrlTabSettingOffUsesStripOrder;
RecentTabsSwitcherViewTest.ReleaseCommitsEscapeCancels and
SteppingBackToTheFirstTabIsLikeEscape; browser:
NumberBadgeTest.CtrlTabEndsWithTheKeyOrTheWindow and
AStripWhoseRunEndedComesDown, each checking the tab on screen stays while
a step moves the run's position.

Why: Arc's Ctrl-Tab works this way, as Cmd-Tab does for apps; GitHub issue
123 asked for it.
Removable when: never as behaviour.
